# Trigger a State change on a PackML Node (Equipment Module).
#
# Unlike a plain service, the result is not returned when the transition is merely
# accepted -- it is returned when the node's own commanded work for `state` has
# genuinely finished (default: immediately after acceptance, matching a node that
# does not override defers_completion()) or failed outright. The action's own
# goal id is the correlation mechanism a manager-side aggregator needs to tell
# "an answer to the cycle I am currently waiting on" apart from a stale or
# superseded one -- no separate generation/sequence field is needed on the wire.

State state

---
# PackML Node Response
bool success    # True if the node's work for `state` completed successfully.
int8 error_code # Error code if the transition was rejected or the work failed.
string message  # Message for display (only for human reading)

# Error Codes
int8 SUCCESS = 1
int8 INVALID_STATE_REQUEST = -1

---
# No feedback defined -- PackML's SC (state complete) signal has no standard
# progress concept; reserved for future use.
